    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d76">

                <pb facs="0346" n="60" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg60"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2943</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Saloniki</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kehl</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Saloniki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-10-13T13:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 13, 1916, 1 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 14, 12
                        noon</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Revolutionists now in complete control of every public office in Saloniki.
                    Belligerent consuls visited Provisional President. If Provisional Government
                    remains here it is presumed that the Consulate may deal with it informally and
                    unofficially when necessary, pending further instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consul</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
